WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.770
Our classroom fan has a rule.

2
00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:06.250
It should run when it's hot and

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.130
someone is in the room.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.660
But a switch can't think.

5
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.780
So how does a machine follow a rule?

6
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.170
Today: switches that decide,

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.150
with AND, OR and NOT.

8
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:25.910
A switch is either on or off.

9
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.420
Computers write on as

10
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.440
one, and off as zero.

11
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.440
Every decision a device makes is built

12
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.480
from ones and zeros like these.

13
00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.510
Put two switches one after the other in

14
00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.250
the loop: that's called series.

15
00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.390
The light comes on only when switch

16
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:47.450
A and switch B are both on.

17
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.360
Turn either off, and the loop breaks.

18
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.170
That's AND.

19
00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.580
Now put them side by side: that's

20
00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.960
parallel, and the current has two paths.

21
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.530
The light comes on when A

22
00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.430
or B is on, or both.

23
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:04.780
That's OR.

24
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:06.720
Quick check!

25
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.820
Two switches in parallel.

26
00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:13.140
Switch A is off, and switch B is on.

27
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.230
Is the lamp on or off?

28
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:16.880
It's on.

29
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.620
Switch B gives the current a

30
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.720
path, so the loop is closed.

31
00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:25.130
With OR, one is enough; with

32
00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.670
AND, you'd need both.

33
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:31.500
The third one is NOT: it flips its input.

34
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:32.960
Think of a fridge.

35
00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.590
A shut door presses a button,

36
00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.250
and the light goes off.

37
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.480
The light is on when the

38
00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.920
button is NOT pressed.

39
00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.430
To check a rule, make a truth table:

40
00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:47.350
every possible input, and the output.

41
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.080
Two switches give four rows.

42
00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.510
For AND, the output is one

43
00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.450
only when both are on.

44
00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.710
Now our fan.

45
00:01:58.400 --> 00:01:59.940
One input comes from a

46
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.960
temperature sensor: is it hot?

47
00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.620
Another comes from a motion

48
00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.660
sensor: is someone in?

49
00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.940
Hot AND someone in turns the fan on.

50
00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.940
And the teacher's own switch joins with

51
00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.840
OR, so she can always switch it on.

52
00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.520
Your turn.

53
00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.630
A pump fills the school tank from a well.

54
00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.060
It should run when the tank is low,

55
00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.280
but never when the well is dry.

56
00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.600
Which rule: low AND NOT

57
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.860
dry, or low OR dry?

58
00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:35.690
Low AND NOT dry: the pump runs only when

59
00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:37.770
the tank needs water and the well has

60
00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:37.970
some.

61
00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.010
Remember: series makes AND,

62
00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.170
parallel makes OR, NOT flips, and a

63
00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.870
truth table checks every case.

64
00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:51.230
Try it yourself: pick a device at home,

65
00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:55.170
like a fridge or a torch, and write its

66
00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:58.610
rule with AND, OR or NOT.

67
00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.430
Then make its truth table.

68
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.700
Got a battery, a bulb and foil?

69
00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.440
Build AND and OR for real.

70
00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:12.570
Next time: counting in ones and zeros.
